---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Agent Authority & Evidence Audit — Decision Scope Intake" description="Prepare a local BitEvo scope brief that seeds an Authority Ledger, Evidence Contract and written Rules of Engagement for one action-capable AI workflow.">
  <section class="intake-hero section-tight"><div class="container hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Decision scope intake</div><h1 class="page-title">Define the action, evidence gate and authority owner before anyone tests it.</h1></div><div><p class="lede">Build the scope locally. Mapper drafts can be handed into this page through browser session storage; nothing here transmits data or authorizes testing.</p></div></div></section>

  <div data-intake-segmentation data-intake-locale="en">
  <section class="section-tight section-rule">
    <div id="mapperHandoff" class="container handoff panel" hidden><div><span>LOCAL MAPPER HANDOFF</span><strong>Technical scope seed loaded from Authority Mapper.</strong><p>Review every imported field. Owner decision, object-binding evidence, Rules-of-Engagement permissions, company/contact, access approval, data boundary and testing authorization remain intentionally unset.</p></div><button id="clearHandoff" type="button" class="button button-ghost">Clear mapper draft</button></div>
    <div class="container warning panel" role="alert"><div class="warning-mark">!</div><div><strong>Do not submit or paste secrets.</strong><p>API keys · passwords · tokens · private keys · wallet seeds · production credentials · customer secrets. Describe boundaries, evidence classes and access paths instead.</p></div></div>

    <div class="container panel" style="max-width:1120px;margin-bottom:18px;padding:20px">
      <div class="eyebrow">Choose intake depth</div>
      <h2 style="margin:6px 0 8px;font-size:1.15rem">Start with Entry. Expand only when the owner decision needs Primary depth.</h2>
      <p data-intake-mode-state style="margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem">ENTRY · reduced first-step fields · Primary evidence/RoE fields deferred until deeper scope review</p>
      <div class="brief-actions">
        <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-intake-mode="entry" aria-pressed="true">Entry depth · reduced first step</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-ghost" data-intake-mode="primary" aria-pressed="false">Primary depth · full intake</button>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:12px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem">Both modes are browser-local. Choosing a depth does not transmit data, book work or authorize testing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="container intake-grid">
      <form id="audit-intake" class="form-shell panel">
        <section class="form-section"><div class="form-section-head"><span>01</span><div><h2>Owner decision</h2><p>Start with the business decision this work must support.</p></div></div><div class="two"><label>Company<input id="company" autocomplete="organization" required placeholder="Company or project" /></label><label>Business contact<input id="contact" autocomplete="name" required placeholder="Name + business contact" /></label></div><label>Role<input id="role" autocomplete="organization-title" required placeholder="CTO / Founder / Engineering Lead / Security Lead" /></label><label>Decision to enable<textarea id="ownerDecision" rows="3" required placeholder="Example: decide whether this workflow should keep, gain or lose write authority"></textarea></label></section>

        <section class="form-section"><div class="form-section-head"><span>02</span><div><h2>Authority Ledger seed</h2><p>Entry captures the consequential action. Primary expands the evidence and operating boundary.</p></div></div><label>Agent / workflow description<textarea id="workflow" rows="3" required placeholder="What the workflow does in one or two sentences"></textarea></label><label>Critical external action<textarea id="criticalAction" rows="3" required placeholder="The exact write / send / update / deploy / mutate action whose failure matters most"></textarea></label><label>Target object / object binding<textarea id="targetObject" rows="3" required placeholder="What exact record, recipient, environment or object may be changed — and how it is identified"></textarea></label><div class="two"><label>Authority owner<input id="authorityOwner" required placeholder="Role that owns permission for this action" /></label><label hidden data-primary-only>Access approver<input id="approver" required data-primary-required placeholder="Role/name authorized to approve audit access" /></label></div><label hidden data-primary-only>External systems / tools<textarea id="externalSystems" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="Tools, APIs, MCP servers and external systems involved — names only, no credentials"></textarea></label><label hidden data-primary-only>Authority that must remain impossible<textarea id="forbiddenEffects" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="Writes, sends, objects, systems or escalation paths this workflow must never be allowed to use"></textarea></label><label>Most expensive plausible error<textarea id="expensiveError" rows="3" required placeholder="Describe the business or operational consequence"></textarea></label><label>Environment<input id="environment" required placeholder="staging / test / isolated lab / other" /></label></section>

        <section class="form-section" hidden data-primary-only><div class="form-section-head"><span>03</span><div><h2>Evidence Contract seed</h2><p>Primary depth: define what must be true before the workflow may create the effect.</p></div></div><label>Pre-action evidence<textarea id="preActionEvidence" rows="4" required data-primary-required placeholder="Inputs, approvals, source state, policy state or other evidence required before action"></textarea></label><label>Freshness / validity rule<textarea id="freshnessRule" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="How current must the evidence be, and what makes it invalid or stale?"></textarea></label><label>Object-binding evidence<textarea id="objectBinding" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="How does the workflow prove evidence and approval apply to the exact target?"></textarea></label><label>External confirmation<textarea id="externalConfirmation" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="What independent read-back, receipt or state observation proves the intended effect actually happened?"></textarea></label><label>Behavior when evidence is missing<textarea id="uncertaintyBehavior" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="Stop / constrain / reconcile / compensate / rollback / escalate"></textarea></label></section>

        <section class="form-section" hidden data-primary-only><div class="form-section-head"><span>04</span><div><h2>Rules of Engagement</h2><p>Primary depth: define what may happen during testing and what must never happen.</p></div></div><div class="two"><label>Test / staging available?<select id="staging" required data-primary-required><option value="">Select</option><option>Yes</option><option>No</option><option>Partial / needs setup</option></select></label><label>Safe replay available?<select id="replay" required data-primary-required><option value="">Select</option><option>Yes</option><option>No</option><option>Unknown</option></select></label></div><label>Allowed tests<textarea id="allowedTests" rows="4" required data-primary-required placeholder="What may be tested, replayed, written or simulated"></textarea></label><label>Prohibited audit actions<textarea id="prohibited" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="Actions, systems, data or effects the audit itself must never touch"></textarea></label></section>

        <section class="form-section" hidden data-primary-only><div class="form-section-head"><span>05</span><div><h2>Data & secret boundary</h2><p>Primary depth: use the minimum evidence necessary for the agreed workflow.</p></div></div><label>Data classification<input id="classification" required data-primary-required placeholder="public / internal / confidential / regulated / other" /></label><label>Minimum necessary data<textarea id="minimumData" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="Smallest dataset/log subset needed for the audit"></textarea></label><label>Secret-handling boundary<textarea id="secretBoundary" rows="3" required data-primary-required placeholder="How credentials and secrets remain outside the audit evidence path"></textarea></label></section>

        <label class="confirm"><input type="checkbox" id="secretConfirm" required /><span>I confirm this form contains no credentials, private keys, wallet seeds or customer secrets. Entry depth still requires this boundary.</span></label>
        <div class="form-actions"><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Generate Entry scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><button class="button button-ghost" type="reset">Reset</button></div>
      </form>

      <aside class="brief-panel panel"><div class="brief-top"><div><div class="eyebrow">Local output</div><h2>Decision scope brief</h2></div><span id="briefState">Not generated</span></div><p class="brief-explain">Entry produces a reduced first-step brief. Primary expands it into the full Authority Ledger + Evidence Contract + Rules-of-Engagement seed. Review before sharing.</p><textarea id="brief" data-segmented-brief readonly aria-label="Generated decision scope brief" placeholder="Complete the required fields, then generate the brief."></textarea><div class="brief-actions"><button id="copy" type="button" class="button" disabled>Copy brief</button><button id="download" type="button" class="button button-ghost" disabled>Download .txt</button></div><div class="gate"><span>AUTHORIZATION GATE</span><strong>Testing authorization: NOT GRANTED by this form.</strong><p>Scope review is not execution permission. Allowed/prohibited actions, access approval, data boundaries and replay conditions must be agreed in writing before testing.</p></div></aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('audit-intake');
    const brief = document.getElementById('brief');
    const copy = document.getElementById('copy');
    const download = document.getElementById('download');
    const briefState = document.getElementById('briefState');
    const handoffNotice = document.getElementById('mapperHandoff');
    const clearHandoff = document.getElementById('clearHandoff');
    const value = id => document.getElementById(id)?.value?.trim() || '-';
    const setValue = (id, v='') => { const el=document.getElementById(id); if (el && v) el.value=v; };
    const setReady = ready => { copy.disabled=!ready; download.disabled=!ready; briefState.textContent=ready?'Ready to review':'Not generated'; };

    const loadMapperHandoff = () => {
      const raw = sessionStorage.getItem('bitevo.mapper.handoff.v1');
      if (!raw) return;
      try {
        const map = JSON.parse(raw); const a=map.authority_ledger||{}; const e=map.evidence_contract||{};
        setValue('workflow', `${a.workflow || 'Mapped workflow'}\nAction class: ${map.action_class || 'custom'}`);
        setValue('criticalAction', a.critical_action); setValue('targetObject', a.target_binding); setValue('authorityOwner', a.authority_owner); setValue('forbiddenEffects', a.prohibited_authority); setValue('expensiveError', a.expensive_error); setValue('environment', a.environment);
        setValue('preActionEvidence', e.pre_action_evidence); setValue('freshnessRule', e.freshness_rule); setValue('externalConfirmation', e.external_confirmation); setValue('uncertaintyBehavior', e.recovery_behavior);
        handoffNotice.hidden=false; briefState.textContent='Mapper seed loaded — owner/RoE confirmation required';
      } catch { sessionStorage.removeItem('bitevo.mapper.handoff.v1'); }
    };
    loadMapperHandoff();
    clearHandoff?.addEventListener('click', () => { sessionStorage.removeItem('bitevo.mapper.handoff.v1'); location.replace('/audit-intake'); });

    form.addEventListener('submit', event => {
      event.preventDefault(); if (!form.reportValidity()) return;
      const lines = [
        '=== BITEVO AGENT AUTHORITY & EVIDENCE AUDIT — DECISION SCOPE ===',`Generated: ${new Date().toISOString()}`,
        'PUBLIC FORM WARNING: no API keys, passwords, tokens, private keys, wallet seeds, production credentials or customer secrets.','Testing authorization: NOT GRANTED by this brief. Written Rules of Engagement required.','',
        '--- OWNER DECISION ---',`Company: ${value('company')}`,`Business contact: ${value('contact')}`,`Role: ${value('role')}`,`Decision to enable: ${value('ownerDecision')}`,'',
        '--- AUTHORITY LEDGER SEED ---',`Agent/workflow: ${value('workflow')}`,`Critical external action: ${value('criticalAction')}`,`Target object / object binding: ${value('targetObject')}`,`Authority owner: ${value('authorityOwner')}`,`Access approver: ${value('approver')}`,`External systems/tools: ${value('externalSystems')}`,`Authority that must remain impossible: ${value('forbiddenEffects')}`,`Most expensive plausible error: ${value('expensiveError')}`,`Environment: ${value('environment')}`,'',
        '--- EVIDENCE CONTRACT SEED ---',`Pre-action evidence: ${value('preActionEvidence')}`,`Freshness / validity rule: ${value('freshnessRule')}`,`Object-binding evidence: ${value('objectBinding')}`,`External confirmation: ${value('externalConfirmation')}`,`Behavior when evidence is missing: ${value('uncertaintyBehavior')}`,'',
        '--- RULES OF ENGAGEMENT SEED ---',`Test/staging available: ${value('staging')}`,`Safe replay available: ${value('replay')}`,`Allowed tests: ${value('allowedTests')}`,`Prohibited audit actions: ${value('prohibited')}`,'',
        '--- DATA & SECRET BOUNDARY ---',`Data classification: ${value('classification')}`,`Minimum necessary data: ${value('minimumData')}`,`Secret-handling boundary: ${value('secretBoundary')}`,'',
        'Secret confirmation: user confirmed no credentials/private keys/wallet seeds/customer secrets were entered.','Requested next step: scope review only; no testing until written approval.'
      ];
      brief.value=lines.join('\n'); setReady(true);
    });
    copy.addEventListener('click', async () => { if (!brief.value) return; await navigator.clipboard.writeText(brief.value); const old=copy.textContent; copy.textContent='Copied'; setTimeout(()=>copy.textContent=old,1400); });
    download.addEventListener('click', () => { if (!brief.value) return; const blob=new Blob([brief.value],{type:'text/plain;charset=utf-8'}); const url=URL.createObjectURL(blob); const a=document.createElement('a'); a.href=url; a.download='bitevo-agent-decision-scope.txt'; a.click(); URL.revokeObjectURL(url); });
    form.addEventListener('reset', () => requestAnimationFrame(() => { brief.value=''; setReady(false); }));
  </script>
  <script is:inline src="/intake-segmentation.js"></script>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intake-hero{padding-top:clamp(62px,8vw,104px)}.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:clamp(40px,8vw,100px);align-items:end}.hero-grid .lede{margin:0}.handoff,.warning{max-width:1120px;margin-bottom:18px}.handoff{padding:18px 20px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:22px;border-color:rgba(127,208,177,.28);background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(24,58,50,.24),rgba(8,16,18,.58))}.handoff span{color:var(--green);font:500 .58rem var(--mono);letter-spacing:.1em}.handoff strong{display:block;margin:5px 0 3px}.handoff p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.76rem}.warning{padding:18px 20px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px 1fr;gap:14px;align-items:start;border-color:rgba(228,139,139,.28);background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(69,29,29,.28),rgba(25,14,15,.32))}.warning-mark{width:28px;height:28px;display:grid;place-items:center;border:1px solid rgba(228,139,139,.4);border-radius:50%;color:var(--red);font:500 .72rem var(--mono)}.warning strong{color:#f1caca}.warning p{margin:3px 0 0;color:#ba9999;font-size:.79rem}.intake-grid{max-width:1120px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.12fr .88fr;gap:18px;align-items:start}.form-shell{padding:0 28px}.form-section{padding:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.form-section-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:34px 1fr;gap:12px;margin-bottom:22px}.form-section-head>span{color:var(--green);font:500 .64rem var(--mono)}.form-section h2{margin:0;font-size:1.05rem}.form-section-head p{margin:4px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.76rem}.two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;margin-bottom:14px;color:#96a29f;font:500 .64rem/1.3 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase}input,textarea,select{width:100%;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:11px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.025);color:var(--ink);padding:11px 12px;font:500 .83rem/1.55 var(--sans);letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;outline:none}input:focus,textarea:focus,select:focus{border-color:rgba(127,208,177,.55);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(127,208,177,.06)}textarea{resize:vertical}.confirm{display:grid;grid-template-columns:18px 1fr;align-items:start;gap:10px;padding:13px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:11px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.5}.confirm input{width:16px;height:16px;margin:2px 0 0;padding:0;accent-color:var(--green)}.form-actions{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:0 0 28px}.brief-panel{position:sticky;top:96px;padding:24px}.brief-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px}.brief-top h2{margin:0;font-size:1.25rem}.brief-top>span{padding:5px 8px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;color:var(--muted);font:500 .56rem var(--mono)}.brief-explain{color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}.brief-panel textarea{min-height:560px;margin-top:8px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.66rem;line-height:1.65}.brief-actions{display:flex;gap:9px;margin-top:12px}.brief-actions button:disabled{opacity:.35}.gate{margin-top:20px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.gate>span{color:var(--gold);font:500 .58rem var(--mono);letter-spacing:.1em}.gate strong{display:block;margin:6px 0;font-size:.8rem}.gate p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem}
  @media(max-width:900px){.hero-grid,.intake-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.brief-panel{position:static}.brief-panel textarea{min-height:380px}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.handoff{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.two{grid-template-columns:1fr}.form-shell{padding:0 18px}.brief-actions{flex-direction:column}.brief-actions .button,.handoff .button{width:100%}}
</style>